In case you stored the repo on your Windows machine and get an 403 error when trying to open http://localhost:4173, it might be because you have a `~` in the path (mine was `C:\Github\~god`, obviously). 

Use the following change to make it work:

```js
vite.config.js

...
export default defineConfig(({ mode, command }) => {
...
    server: {
...
      fs: {
        // Vite 6 rejects Windows paths containing `~` before consulting `allow`.
        strict: false,
      },
    },
```

