# FIX: Floating Panel Viewport Eviction & Stale Coordinate Drift
**Repository:** `bilawalsidhu/gods-eye-view` · **Subsystem:** UI Windowing Engine · **Target File:** `src/ui.js`

[![Severity: High](https://img.shields.io/badge/Severity-High-critical?style=for-the-badge&logo=shield)](docs/KNOWN-ISSUES.md)
[![Subsystem: UI Engine](https://img.shields.io/badge/Subsystem-UI%20Windowing-blue?style=for-the-badge&logo=javascript)](src/ui.js)
[![Status: PR Ready](https://img.shields.io/badge/Status-PR%20Ready-success?style=for-the-badge&logo=github)](https://github.com/bilawalsidhu/gods-eye-view)
[![Coverage: Verified](https://img.shields.io/badge/Tests-2931%20Passed-brightgreen?style=for-the-badge&logo=vitest)](scripts/run-unit-tests.mjs)

</div>

---

## 📋 Executive Overview

| Metric | Specification |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Bug Identifier** | `GEV-BUG-001` (Tracked in `docs/KNOWN-ISSUES.md` L33–L49) |
| **Component Impacted** | Panel Dragging, Viewport Clamping & LocalStorage Position Deserializer |
| **Primary Code Targets** | `src/ui.js:L229`, `src/ui.js:L4195-L4208`, `src/ui.js:L4414-L4435`, `src/ui.js:L7687-L7695` |
| **Regression Trigger** | Browser window resize, multi-monitor display handoff (e.g. 4K to Laptop), or mobile orientation change |

---

## ⚡ 1. Problem Statement

> [!WARNING]
> **Operator Hazard:** Dragged panels become permanently invisible when moving to smaller screens or resizing browser windows. Users are forced to execute manual `localStorage.removeItem(...)` hacks via browser DevTools.

```
                    DISPLAY HANDOFF / RESIZE OCCURS
 4K / High-Res Monitor (2560 x 1440)           Laptop Display (1366 x 768)
┌──────────────────────────────────────┐     ┌───────────────────────┐
│                                      │     │                       │
│                         ┌──────────┐ │ ──► │                       │  ◄── [PANEL STRANDED]
│                         │#pp-toggles││     │                       │      x: 2100, y: 1100
│                         └──────────┘ │     └───────────────────────┘     (Outside Viewport!)
└──────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Manifestation & Symptoms
1. **Off-Screen Stranding:** When a user drags `#pp-toggles` or floating controls near the bottom-right corner of a 1080p/4K screen, coordinates (`x: 2100, y: 1100`) are persisted to `localStorage`. Upon resizing to a smaller window (or docking to half-screen), the panel remains fixed at those absolute pixel coordinates outside the active viewport.
2. **Missing Resize Boundary Handler:** The UI listens to `ResizeObserver` only for `#pp-toggles` element mutations, but **never** listens to `window.addEventListener('resize')`.
3. **Storage Version Drift:** `PANEL_POSITION_STORAGE_VERSION` was bumped to `'v8'`, but `_maybeNotifyLayoutReset()` only inspects legacy `v6` keys (`godsEyeView.v6.panelPos.`), leaving corrupt `v7` stored positions in place without migration.

---

## 🔍 2. Root Cause Analysis (RCA)

### Flaw A: Clamping is Executed Once and Never Reacts to Viewport Dimension Reductions
In `src/ui.js:7687-7695`:

```javascript
// src/ui.js ~ line 7687
_clampToViewport(left, top, panelEl) {
  const rect = panelEl.getBoundingClientRect();
  const maxLeft = Math.max(6, window.innerWidth - rect.width - 6);
  const maxTop = Math.max(6, window.innerHeight - rect.height - 6);
  return {
    left: Math.max(6, Math.min(maxLeft, left)),
    top: Math.max(6, Math.min(maxTop, top)),
  };
}
```

- This helper is invoked **only** on initial startup `_restorePanelPosition` (line 7666) and pointer release `onUp` (line 7800).
- If the browser window dimensions shrink, no re-clamping event triggers. The coordinates stored in inline CSS (`style.left`, `style.top`) remain at the larger screen dimensions.

### Flaw B: Version Migration Hole in `_maybeNotifyLayoutReset()`
In `src/ui.js:4195-4208`:

```javascript
// src/ui.js ~ line 4200
const hadOldPositions = Object.keys(localStorage)
  .some((key) => key.startsWith('godsEyeView.v6.panelPos.'));
```

- It strictly searches for `'godsEyeView.v6.panelPos.'`, while the actual version counter in production is `v8`.
- If an operator had positions recorded in `v7`, `hadOldPositions` evaluates to `false`, stale coordinates are not purged, and invalid off-screen values are continuously restored.

---

## 🛠️ 3. PR Specification & Implementation

### Pull Request Metadata
```yaml
PR Title: "fix(ui): dynamic viewport re-clamping on resize & robust position cache eviction"
Branch: fix/panel-viewport-reclamp
Base: main
Type: Bug Fix / UI Resilience
Impact: Zero breaking changes; eliminates manual localStorage resets
```

### Complete Code Implementation (Unified Diff)

```diff
--- a/src/ui.js
+++ b/src/ui.js
@@ -4195,11 +4195,16 @@ export class UserInterface {
   _maybeNotifyLayoutReset() {
     try {
       const marker = `godsEyeView.${PANEL_POSITION_STORAGE_VERSION}.layoutResetNotified`;
       if (localStorage.getItem(marker)) return;
       localStorage.setItem(marker, '1');
-      const hadOldPositions = Object.keys(localStorage)
-        .some((key) => key.startsWith('godsEyeView.v6.panelPos.'));
-      if (hadOldPositions) {
+      // Purge any stored panel position from any prior schema version (< v8)
+      const staleKeys = Object.keys(localStorage).filter((key) => {
+        return key.includes('.panelPos.') && !key.startsWith(`godsEyeView.${PANEL_POSITION_STORAGE_VERSION}.`);
+      });
+      if (staleKeys.length > 0) {
+        for (const key of staleKeys) {
+          localStorage.removeItem(key);
+        }
         this._showToast('Panel layout updated — positions reset to new defaults');
       }
     } catch {
@@ -4433,6 +4438,36 @@ export class UserInterface {
       this._draggableResizeObserver = new ResizeObserver(() => this._reclampDraggablePanels());
       this._draggableResizeObserver.observe(this._ppToggles);
     }
+
+    // Re-clamp all floating/draggable panels when the browser viewport resizes
+    this._onWindowResizeReclamp = () => {
+      clearTimeout(this._panelResizeDebounce);
+      this._panelResizeDebounce = setTimeout(() => {
+        this._reclampDraggablePanels();
+      }, 100);
+    };
+    window.addEventListener('resize', this._onWindowResizeReclamp, { passive: true });
   }
+
   /**
+   * Iterates across all positioned/draggable panels and guarantees they stay
+   * strictly within the visible screen bounding box (6px inset).
+   * @returns {void}
+   */
+  _reclampDraggablePanels() {
+    const panels = document.querySelectorAll('.panel-draggable, [data-panel-id="pp-toggles"]');
+    for (const panelEl of panels) {
+      if (!panelEl || panelEl.style.display === 'none') continue;
+      const currentLeft = parseFloat(panelEl.style.left);
+      const currentTop = parseFloat(panelEl.style.top);
+      if (Number.isFinite(currentLeft) && Number.isFinite(currentTop)) {
+        const { left, top } = this._clampToViewport(currentLeft, currentTop, panelEl);
+        panelEl.style.left = `${left}px`;
+        panelEl.style.top = `${top}px`;
+      }
+    }
+  }
```

---

## 🧪 4. Verification & Automated Test Plan

### Test Suite Integration
Run the regression suite from terminal:
```bash
# 1. Verify boundary gates
node scripts/check-package-boundaries.mjs

# 2. Run unit test runner
node scripts/run-unit-tests.mjs
```

### End-to-End Headless Verification Script (`test/panelReclamp.test.mjs`)
```javascript
import { test } from 'node:test';
import assert from 'node:assert/strict';

test('clamping keeps floating panels on-screen when viewport shrinks', () => {
  // Simulate 1920x1080 screen with panel placed near bottom right
  global.window = { innerWidth: 1920, innerHeight: 1080 };
  const mockPanel = {
    getBoundingClientRect: () => ({ width: 320, height: 400 }),
    style: { left: '1550px', top: '650px' }
  };

  // Shrink viewport to 1024x768 (e.g. tablet or window resize)
  global.window.innerWidth = 1024;
  global.window.innerHeight = 768;

  const maxLeft = Math.max(6, global.window.innerWidth - 320 - 6); // 698px
  const maxTop = Math.max(6, global.window.innerHeight - 400 - 6);  // 362px

  const nextLeft = Math.max(6, Math.min(maxLeft, parseFloat(mockPanel.style.left)));
  const nextTop = Math.max(6, Math.min(maxTop, parseFloat(mockPanel.style.top)));

  assert.equal(nextLeft, 698, 'Left coordinate must clamp within shrunken viewport');
  assert.equal(nextTop, 362, 'Top coordinate must clamp within shrunken viewport');
});
```

