5. Repeat step 3–4 with `height: 1500, pitch: -55` for the contrast case.

**How firmly this reproduces, stated exactly:** I got it on the one run I was able to make against `main` on this GPU — the 650 m / −30° arrival buried all 6000 dots, the 1500 m / −55° arrival in the same run was clean. Separately, in a headless SwiftShader context, two of four test cameras showed the same signature (dots at −16825 m), so it is not specific to this GPU or driver. I tried to run it a second time on `main` before filing and could not: `overpass-api.de` is currently returning 406 to my network, so the layer never loads roads. Please treat the counts above as one observation per environment rather than a measured rate.

I have deliberately not proposed a patch, since the fix is a design call: re-sample per road, reject a sample that is implausibly far from the globe surface at that coordinate, or defer road construction until the tiles under the probe have resolved. Happy to implement whichever direction you prefer.

